            <ArticleTitle>Difficulty walking. A presentation of idiopathic juvenile osteoporosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>173-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Idiopathic juvenile osteoporosis is a rare condition that may present as difficulty walking. Difficulty walking represents a challenging differential diagnosis in pediatrics. Diagnostic studies are usually oriented to rule out neuromuscular etiologies or, once organic causes have been reasonably discarded, conversion disorders. We describe 2 patients who presented with difficulty or inability to walk due to idiopathic juvenile osteoporosis, a rare disease unfamiliar to most physicians. However, early diagnosis in patients can avoid extensive testing and prolonged hospitalizations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
